request: Make the output easier to read.

governor turn 1: ask  ("Easier to read" could mean several different changes to the format unit's output, and existing tests pin the current format. I need a concrete target before I can write a testable contract and decide which existing tests may change.)
governor asks: Which of these changes to the todo list output do you want? Pick any that apply, or describe your own:
1. Status markers: show "[ ]" for open todos and "[x]" for done ones, e.g. "[ ] 3  Buy milk".
2. Aligned columns: pad IDs and titles so the status, ID, title and due date line up vertically.
3. Due dates: show them in a consistent form, e.g. "(due 2024-05-01)", and maybe flag overdue items.
4. Grouping and sorting: open todos before done ones, or sorted by due date.
5. A header line and/or a summary footer, e.g. "3 open, 2 done".
6. An empty-list message, e.g. "No todos.", instead of blank output.
Also, should this affect only the list output, or the confirmation messages printed after add and complete too?

